/E (Database languages are divided based on their roles: Data Definition Language \(DDL\) focuses on building, modifying, and managing the overall structure of a database, while Data Manipulation Language \(DML\) handles the actual data stored inside those structures by allowing users to add, edit, delete, and retrieve records. This lab provided hands-on practice with CREATE, INSERT, UPDATE, and SELECT statements, and helped build a clearer understanding of how data can be manipulated and queried within a MySQL database using phpMyAdmin. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
>>
